Subject: [PATCH] Sexidium linearstats command hooks (L2-STATS)

Loop-2 Stage 2 (SUM): Paper-side hooks for the Linear timing stats.
(1) PaperCommands static-block registration anchoring on the tps line.
(2) CommandLinearStats (Bukkit Command, mirrors CommandServerHealth shape).
(3) LinearRegionFlushCompletedEvent (ASYNC super(true), flush-granularity) +
Paper-side bridge firing it OFF IO threads via the async scheduler, only when
>=1 file attempted. Command output is pull-only via coordinator snapshots() /
sexidium$stats(); no new storage fields, no NMS signature changes.
(4) SexidiumLinearFolderNames (single shared helper for folderType/world,
de-duplicated from command + bridge; folderType pinned region|poi|entities).

BASE-TREE ASSUMPTIONS (Folia base checkout absent locally at
/tmp/sexidium-folia; all Paper hunks are written against stated assumed
context and must be re-checked by the integrator — see return message):
(A1) PaperCommands.java is the legacy Bukkit-style registry with a static
COMMANDS map and a `COMMANDS.put("tps", ...)` line (if base is
brigadier-only, adapt to BasicCommand registration instead).
(A2) CommandServerHealth shape is `extends org.bukkit.command.Command` with
ctor/execute/empty-tabComplete (mirrored here; relocate package to match
its real location if different). Permission `sexidium.command.linearstats`
defaults to OP, mirrored from tps in code; if base declares tps in
permissions.yml/default-OP instead, integrator must mirror the
permissions.yml entry there too (see Command javadoc + code comment).
(A3) Event package `org.bukkit.event.world` exists with HandlerList pattern
(if base uses io.papermc.paper.event, relocate accordingly). Event is ASYNC
(`super(true)` + javadoc contract; region-scheduler sync delivery was
considered and rejected for this stats-only signal — see event javadoc for
contract + 5-line listener sample).
(A4) Async scheduler API (`Bukkit.getAsyncScheduler`) exists as on 26.x
(fallback: documented sync fire with a comment if absent; region scheduler
is NOT used for delivery — async was chosen for Folia-safe off-IO fire).
(A5) notifyFlush CALL-SITE ASSUMPTION (explicit, Paper-side save path, integrator to wire):
this patch provides `SexidiumLinearFlushBridge#notifyFlush(Plugin,String,long,long)`
but NO call site; the integrator must wire it into the Paper-side save path
(e.g., after `LinearFlushCoordinator.flushDirty()` in world save), passing
the owning `Plugin` explicitly (the old `getProvidingPlugin(Bridge.class)`
misuse is fixed via param; do NOT use it — the bridge class lives in
server code, not a plugin jar). If the assumed save path moved, adapt the
wiring, not the bridge contract.

